direction: down

title: |md
  ## ARP table (arp_tbl) layout
| {near: top-center; shape: text}

table: "struct neigh_table arp_tbl\n(net/ipv4/arp.c:152)\n\nHash table of neighbour entries:\n- Key: IP address + dev pointer\n- Value: struct neighbour (MAC + state)\n\nMemory accounting:\n- gc_thresh1 (low water mark)\n- gc_thresh2 (soft limit)\n- gc_thresh3 (hard limit; refuse new entries)\n\nnet.ipv4.neigh.default.*\nDefaults: 128 / 512 / 1024.\nHeavy traffic often raises." {
  style.fill: "#dbeafe"
}

operations: "Operations\n\n- neigh_lookup(arp_tbl, &ip, dev)\n   returns struct neighbour * (refcounted)\n- neigh_create()\n   inserts INCOMPLETE entry,\n   triggers ARP request\n- neigh_update()\n   on ARP reply, updates HA + state\n- neigh_event_send()\n   per-skb path; queues if not yet resolved\n- garbage collection (timer-driven)\n   reclaims old entries" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
}

userspace: "Inspect/manipulate\n\nip neigh show\nip neigh add 10.0.0.1\n   lladdr aa:bb:cc... dev eth0\nip neigh flush all\n\n/proc/net/arp (legacy view)\n/proc/sys/net/ipv4/neigh/eth0/*\n   (per-iface tunables)" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
}

table -> operations
operations -> userspace
